A||N||4||Fiero_Freak||DIS Spark Adv Problem||||1||
Z||000000||Fiero_Freak||10-18-2001||11:08 PM||||HELP!!!   What all inputs into the ECM to control the spark advance?  This is on an 87 coupe with 5-speed.  It has the DIS ignition system.   It will begin advancing the spark, but too far on the throttle, or load, and the advance drops back to 30 deg....  so you basically can't go any faster.  I thought it could be the TPS so I replaced and it made the problem "crisper".  New wires....getting spark...no timing to set.  I used the code scanner to watch the advance go up to 50 something degrees and then drop off.  It doesn't drop off at a certain degree that varies too.   Could it possibly be the MAP sensor?<BR>If you have any other thoughts I could sure use them.  Or if you know what other reading go into advancing the spark let me know.  Thanks<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero_Left_01.jpg"> <BR>Two '87 GT's...<BR>   ...Double Trouble||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||10-19-2001||08:33 PM||||Make sure the MAP sensor is hooked up right and the line is clear and sealed tight. check all other vac lines. <P>clamp all PCV line joints. (Gentle with that. the rubber is soft. Overtight will ruin it.)<P>MAP is the main thing controlling advance sensor wise the rest is done by the ECM based on RPM and other things.<P>Ignore spark advance on the scanner. It's meaningless as far as what you are doing. By the time the scanner displays it the number is several RPM behind real time.<P>I would replace the MAP, ECT, and MAT. Make sure you get good sensors. Borg Warner or ACDelco are all I'll use on those three. Most others either aren't made right/well.<P>Also make sure the exhaust manifold hasn't cracked.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero_Freak||10-20-2001||12:37 AM||||   Not the MAP sensor.  Tried that tonight with one that works.  So why won't the scanner help?  It is as least telling me that for some reason the timinng is getting advanced, and then with a little more push on the throttle, losing all the advance. That much I can accually feel right when I see it happen on the scanner.  Could it accually be the computer?  BTW...what is the ECT?||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-20-2001||08:29 PM||||Sensor names... in my cave... sensor QRG... <P>MAP function isn't the only issue. MAP MUST be connected to correct TBI vac port or Manifold vacuum directly. The line must be good and tightly sealed. Preferably as short as posible as well. That plastic line is great for cracking....<P>Trust me.... DIS can be really picky about MAP sensors. I had a new sensor that would make mine stumble when I punched it. Replaced that with a new BWD one and it's run perfectly since.<P>Scanner is no good because the ECM changes timing with each plug firing. Scanner number means very little. Timing can change 20* between firings. Scanner only updates a couple times a second.<P>You also need to go over everything for vac leaks and make sure all lines connect to correct ports. <P>Fuel vapor canister must be working and connected correctly or it will cause problems. If you aren't sure plug both vac lines at the TBI...<P>I doubt this is an ECM problem. It could be a crappy connector someplace. batty ground will also do odd things. Check all the wires bolted to the block and bell housing. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fiero_Freak||10-22-2001||01:12 PM||||Ended up being a coil.  I don't really understand that one....but ok.  I would think it would either work, not work, or just be weak.  It wasn't RPM related, more load related. Either way, it works now.  Thanks for your help.<P>||||reg||1
